hyprshutdown: exit 2 when the user cancels, and always deliver the status

hyprshutdown exits 0 whether every app closed, the user forced them closed or
the user pressed Cancel, so a caller that runs a reboot or power off after it
(with --no-exit) can't tell a cancel from a finish. Its log can't settle it
either: Cancel logs nothing, the last 150 ms check can already read zero apps,
and app classes are logged verbatim, so a class containing a newline can forge
log lines. Exit 2 on Cancel, and 1 when the UI backend fails to start (the
status was ignored before), so the outcome comes from something app text
can't touch.

Once the UI has run, returning from main runs mesa's exit handlers, which
segfault on some exits (glsl_type_singleton_decref freeing into a corrupted
heap) and replace the status with SIGSEGV. End with _Exit after flushing
stdout instead, so the status always reaches the caller.

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@
 #include <hyprutils/cli/ArgumentParser.hpp>
 #include <hyprutils/os/Process.hpp>
 
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <print>
 
 using namespace Hyprutils::OS;
@@ -91,7 +93,7 @@
     // Capture VT switch option before running UI
     auto vtSwitch = parser.getInt("vt");
 
-    g_ui->run();
+    const bool RAN = g_ui->run();
 
     // VT switch for NVIDIA+SDDM: after Hyprland exits, the display may not
     // automatically switch back to the greeter's VT, causing a black screen.
@@ -103,5 +105,13 @@
         proc.runAsync();
     }
 
-    return 0;
+    // Exit 0 for every ending would make Cancel indistinguishable from apps closing; a
+    // caller deciding whether to go on and reboot needs a status app text can't forge.
+    const int STATUS = !RAN ? 1 : g_ui->m_cancelled ? 2 : 0;
+
+    // Once the UI has run, mesa's exit handlers (glsl_type_singleton_decref) free into a
+    // corrupted heap and segfault on some exits, which loses this status. Nothing is left
+    // to clean up that the kernel won't, so skip them.
+    std::fflush(stdout);
+    std::_Exit(STATUS);
 }
diff --git a/src/ui/UI.cpp b/src/ui/UI.cpp
--- a/src/ui/UI.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/UI.cpp
@@ -208,6 +208,10 @@
 }
 
 void CUI::exit(bool closeHl) {
+    // a timer tick can still land between Cancel and the backend going away; it must not
+    // turn a cancel back into a finish
+    if (!closeHl)
+        m_cancelled = true;
     g_ui->m_states.clear();
 
     g_ui->backend()->addIdle([this, closeHl] {
diff --git a/src/ui/UI.hpp b/src/ui/UI.hpp
--- a/src/ui/UI.hpp
+++ b/src/ui/UI.hpp
@@ -70,6 +70,8 @@
     bool                       m_noExit = false;
     std::optional<std::string> m_postExitCmd;
     std::string                m_shutdownLabel;
+    // set when the run ends without closing Hyprland, so main can report a cancel
